    "constraints": [
      "The grammatical concept and examples are provided in this prose: <h1>Nouns in Spanish: Number</h1>\\n<p>In Spanish, nouns can be either <strong>singular</strong> or <strong>plural</strong>. A <em>singular noun</em> refers to one item, while a <em>plural noun</em> refers to more than one item. Understanding the difference between singular and plural is important for proper communication.</p>\\n<h2>Singular Nouns</h2>\\n<ul>\\n    <li><strong>el libro</strong> (the book)</li>\\n    <li><strong>la casa</strong> (the house)</li>\\n    <li><strong>el perro</strong> (the dog)</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h2>Plural Nouns</h2>\\n<ul>\\n    <li><strong>los libros</strong> (the books)</li>\\n    <li><strong>las casas</strong> (the houses)</li>\\n    <li><strong>los perros</strong> (the dogs)</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>To form the plural in Spanish, you usually add <strong>-s</strong> or <strong>-es</strong> to the singular form. For example, <strong>libro</strong> becomes <strong>libros</strong> and <strong>casa</strong> becomes <strong>casas</strong>.</p> ",
      "the sentence should be extracted from the prose examples.",
      "extract accurately, without adding vocabulary thats not in the prose. this is first contact.",
      "conceptual example: 'x es masculino.' or 'y es femenino.'",
      "limit the vocabulary to whats used in the prose."
    ]
  }
